# Mystical Terrain

A Fabric biome mod for Minecraft 1.21.11. It adds 1041 new biomes to the overworld, 12 to the End and 6 to the Nether through TerraBlender, plus 405 kinds of grand tree that replace vanilla's trees outright, from forest giants to world trees, and 200 new blocks with realistic 32x textures that the realms are built from. It also makes the world bigger: biomes and landmasses are four times as wide as vanilla's, and the world runs 67 million blocks out from the centre instead of 30 million. Its biomes go in through TerraBlender, so it still sits next to Biomes O' Plenty, Oh The Biomes We've Gone and other TerraBlender mods, but it has to be installed on the server and on every player's game (see [A bigger world](#a-bigger-world)).

## Realms

The 264 fantasy biomes are grouped into 12 realms. Each realm is its own TerraBlender region: it keeps the vanilla biome layout but swaps around 20 vanilla biomes for its own versions and adds two cave biomes. So you'll cross into an autumn region, then a frost region, with vanilla, BOP or BWG land in between.

| Realm | Biomes | Feel |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Mystical | 14 | The original set: Titan Peaks, Ancient Redwoods, Volcanic Isles and friends. |
| Autumn | 23 | Orange and red canopies, maples, pumpkin fields and leaf litter everywhere. |
| Frost | 23 | Blue-white grass, rime-covered spruces, ice spires, glaciers and floe seas. |
| Ember | 23 | Ash-grey land, charred trees, basalt spires, magma fissures and lava pools, and seas floored with glowing vent fields. |
| Fae | 22 | Lavender grass, blossom-leaved birches and azaleas, amethyst and glowing mushrooms. |
| Primeval | 23 | Deep green jungles and giant conifers, ferns, moss, mud and fossil spires. |
| Twilight | 22 | Dusky blue-purple forests, pale oaks, ghost birches, sculk and eyeblossoms. |
| Tropical | 23 | Turquoise water, palms on the beaches, mango trees, coral lagoons and prismarine. |
| Mire | 23 | Mud, willows and cypresses, lily pads, reed flats and frogspawn caves. |
| Dune | 23 | Sand seas, red-rock canyons, hoodoos, date palms, olive groves and cacti. |
| Fungal | 22 | Mycelium everywhere, mushroom trees, crimson and warped fungus forests. |
| Arcane | 23 | End stone, chorus plants, purpur spires, prismarine seas and amethyst peaks. |

