Each biome takes the place of a vanilla biome in its realm (a realm's forest replaces vanilla forest, its desert replaces desert and so on), and inherits that biome's climate, mobs, structures and surface. On top of that it has its own grass, foliage, water and sky colors, trees, ground blocks, flowers and plants, and rock features.

Each realm is dressed in its own blocks: a wood set with its leaves, a stone, a soil and a couple of plants (see [Blocks](#blocks)).

## Heartland

The other 759 biomes are meant to feel like vanilla: the same trees, flowers and blocks, recombined. Every one is a vanilla biome with one or two twists taken from a shared set of traits:

- Ground and stone: Rocky, Mossy, Gravelly, Sandy, Muddy, Red, Chalk, Granite, Andesite, Diorite, Tuff.
- Season and climate: Snowy, Icy, Autumn, Dry, Lush, Marshy (ponds, reeds and mud), Windswept.
- Trees: Sparse, Dense, Wooded, Old Growth, and mixes like Birch, Spruce, Pine, Oak, Cherry, Pale, Azalea, Acacia, Dark (dark oak), Mangrove or Mixed.
- Plants: Flowering, a single flower (Poppy, Tulip, Daisy, Cornflower, Allium, Bluet, Lily, Orchid, Rose, Lilac, Peony, Wildflower, Petal, Sunflower), Berry, Pumpkin, Melon, Fern, Firefly, Mushroom, Shrubby.
- Water: Kelp Forests, Seagrass Meadows, Reefs, Iceberg Oceans; caves get Ice, Calcite, Granite, Flooded, Azalea and more.

A variant keeps its vanilla biome's mobs, structures, surface and climate (Snowy ones are colder), so a Red Desert still gets desert villages and pyramids and a Wooded Plains still gets plains villages. They're spread over 20 Heartland regions. A region replaces about 30 vanilla biomes and leaves the rest alone, and where it has two versions of the same biome it splits them the way vanilla splits Plains and Sunflower Plains: one on each side of the weirdness noise.

