## Depths

Twelve seas and caves modelled on real places. They have no region of their own: each sea is dealt into six of the Heartland regions and every Heartland region gets two of the caves, in the driest third of its underground, so they turn up all over the world.

| Biome | Replaces | What's there |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Sponge Reef | Deep Cold Ocean | Vases and mounds of sponge on gravel and clay, like the glass-sponge reefs of the Pacific. No kelp this deep. |
| Whale Fall Deep | Deep Ocean | Dark ooze of mud and clay, the odd whale skeleton of bone blocks lying on it, and very dark water. |
| Seamount Pinnacles | Deep Lukewarm Ocean | Stone pinnacles up to 34 blocks tall rising off the seabed, boulders, kelp and coral. |
| Sunken Forest | Ocean | Bare trunks of a drowned forest still standing in mud and dirt among the seagrass. |
| Bioluminescent Bay | Lukewarm Ocean | Sand thick with sea pickles, teal water and a faint glow in the air. |
| Dropstone Shelf | Deep Frozen Ocean | Gravel, clay and bare stone strewn with granite, diorite and andesite boulders dropped by the ice. |
| Limestone Caverns | cave | Calcite and dripstone, great stalagmites and stalactites, water springing from the walls. |
| Glowworm Grotto | cave | Ceilings strung with glow lichen and glow berries over moss, clay and still water. |
| Lava Tubes | cave | Basalt and smooth basalt walls, a floor cracked with magma between obsidian, lava lakes. |
| Guano Roost | cave | A bat colony over coarse dirt and packed mud, mushrooms and hanging roots. |
| Ironstone Caverns | cave | Granite and red sand, iron ore seams in the walls and the odd block of raw iron. |
| Cascade Caverns | cave | Water pouring out of the walls in dozens of falls onto clay, gravel and moss. |

## Grand Trees

Vanilla trees no longer generate in vanilla biomes or in ours: every forest, jungle, taiga and swamp is grown from the mod's own trees, and azalea trees are gone too. Saplings still grow vanilla trees, other mods' biomes keep their own trees, and the Nether's huge fungi are untouched.

Grand trees need real ground under them: one never takes root in another tree's crown or on its branches, including trees whose crowns are mushroom caps, froglights or ice. Their roots follow the slope they stand on instead of jutting out over it, and buttress roots stay low, thick and curved. Banyans hold their crowns up on separate prop roots rather than curtains of them.

**Undergrowth.** Between the trees, every land biome (vanilla's included) now has an understorey to suit it: leafy bushes grown from the local wood and leaves, fallen logs with moss and mushrooms on them, leaf litter under broadleaf woods, bush and berry shrubs, ferns and long grass, mushrooms in damp woods and fireflies by the water. Dry realms get dry grass instead, and the jungle gets the most of all.

There are 405 kinds of grand tree.

**316 grown species.** Every one has its own genes: how many masses its crown splits into and how far they spread, how flat they are, how its trunk bends and forks, whether its branches reach up or droop, how thick its buttresses are, how far its leaves drip. Their branches aren't drawn from a template but grown toward the shape of the crown (space colonization), so they fill it in three dimensions the way real branches compete for light, and no two trees of the same species come out alike. They come in two families and a set of palms:

- **Canopy trees**: one enormous dome of leaves on a thick, buttressed trunk, lumpy on top, hollow underneath where you can see the limbs holding it up, with leaves dripping from its rim.
- **Layered trees**: trunks that snake up in S-bends and throw out long, crooked limbs carrying flat, layered pads of foliage, like ancient pines and giant bonsai.
- **Palms**: 12 kinds, growing on sand beside water on beaches, in deserts, savannas, badlands and jungles.

They come in three sizes:

- **172 forest trees**, 27 to 51 blocks tall and up to about 30 across. These make up the forests themselves: 1 to 2 per chunk in forests, jungles, taigas and swamps (more in Dense and Old Growth variants), a scattering on plains, meadows and savannas.
- **105 grand trees**, 45 to 82 tall and up to about 40 across, rising over the forest here and there.
- **27 colossi**, 82 to 165 tall and up to 140 across, placed as structures about one every 300 blocks where the biome suits them. Find them with `/locate structure mysticalterrain:<name>`.

Vanilla and Heartland biomes get species made of vanilla wood and leaves, each in the biomes it belongs to (oaks in forests and plains, pines in taigas, acacias in savannas and so on); a Heartland variant also grows the species its name promises, so a Cherry Forest grows cherries and an Autumn Taiga autumn trees. The fantasy realms grow their own.

